            <ArticleTitle>ANTICOAGULANT THERAPY IN CORONARY ARTERY DISEASE: A THERAPEUTIC ENIGMA.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>70-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors' experience with anticoagulant therapy in both the acute phase and the long-term management of myocardial infarction has proved disappointing. A review of the literature has failed to establish benefit when all patients with coronary artery disease are treated with anticoagulant drugs. A need for well-controlled studies still exists.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
